The Rust oracle for std's Unicode tables: prints tests/std/unicode/reference-rust.txt,
every scalar value's width and width_cjk (unicode-width 0.2.2; `w START END W WCJK`,
-1 for None), Rust std's char properties (`p START END FLAGS`: alphabetic 1, numeric 2,
whitespace 4, lowercase 8, uppercase 16, control 32) and case mappings (`l`/`u CP M...`).
Regenerate (offline, crates from ~/.cargo): CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/tmp/uo cargo run --release --offline > ../../unicode/reference-rust.txt
